000,"draft_expenses":54407000000,"adjusted_expenses":49507000000},{"year":2026,"draft_revenue":29705000000,"adjusted_revenue":29705000000,"draft_expenses":27169000000,"adjusted_expenses":27169000000}],"adjusted_quarters":{"n":7,"of":25},"flags":[{"type":"circular_financing","origin":"ai","summary":"Intel reports customer deposits and supplier prepayments in the same period, with $1.7 billion of customer deposits supporting future supply and $934 million prepaid to suppliers.","period_end":"2026-06-27"},{"type":"off_balance_sheet","origin":"ai","summary":"Intel reports an unrecognized $29.0 billion commitment for its share of Arizona SCIP construction costs while Arizona SCIP assets are restricted to the VIE's obligations.","period_end":"2024-06-29"},{"type":"off_balance_sheet","origin":"ai","summary":"Intel reports $1.5 billion of first-six-month 2023 receivables sold under non-recourse factoring arrangements.","period_end":"2023-09-30"},{"type":"one_time_dressing","origin":"ai","summary":"Intel reports customer incentives contributing approximately $1.0 billion to Q2 2022 revenue and approximately $900 million to Q1 2023 revenue.","period_end":"2023-04-01"},{"type":"one_time_dressing","origin":"ai","summary":"Intel reports a $1.1 billion special McAfee dividend and $228 million from a partial sale in 2021 investment results.","period_end":"2021-12-25"},{"type":"redefinition","origin":"ai","summary":"The commercial-paper authorization remains $10.0 billion, while later filings separately report drawn commercial paper and changing credit-facility commitments.","period_end":"2025-06-28"},{"type":"related_party_exposure","origin":"ai","summary":"Intel reports recurring receivables and service reimbursements with the deconsolidated NAND OpCo Business.","period_end":"2022-12-31"},{"type":"related_party_exposure","origin":"ai","summary":"Intel reports $3.2 billion invested in related-party Altera and $320 million of wafer-manufacturing revenue from Altera in the first six months of 2026.","period_end":"2026-06-27"},{"type":"subsequent_event","origin":"ai","summary":"The FY2025 filing reports that Intel subsequently received $922 million from a July 11, 2025 Mobileye secondary offering.","period_end":"2025-06-28"},{"type":"subsequent_event","origin":"ai","summary":"The FY2026 first-quarter filing reports Intel's April 8, 2026 acquisition of Apollo's 49% Ireland SCIP interest for $14.2 billion.","period_end":"2026-03-28"},{"type":"subsequent_event","origin":"ai","summary":"The FY2026 first-quarter filing reports an April 2026 draw of $6.5 billion under a senior unsecured term loan facility.","period_end":"2026-03-28"},{"type":"value_revision","origin":"ai","summary":"The FY2020 filing reports SG&A of $6.35 billion for the comparative period versus $6.15 billion in the FY2019 filing.","period_end":"2019-12-28"},{"type":"value_revision","origin":"ai","summary":"The FY2023 filing reports operating cash flow of $29.456 billion for FY2021 versus $29.991 billion in the FY2022 filing.","period_end":"2021-12-25"},{"type":"value_revision","origin":"ai","summary":"The FY2024 filing reports revenue of $24.664 billion for the six months ended July 2, 2022 versus $33.674 billion in the FY2022 filing.","period_end":"2022-07-02"},{"type":"value_revision","origin":"ai","summary":"The FY2024 filing reports an operating loss of $2.484 billion for the six months ended July 2, 2022 versus operating income of $3.641 billion in the FY2022 filing.","period_end":"2022-07-02"}],"narratives":[{"period_end":"2025-09-27","narrative":"Intel reported receipt of $500 million of deferred Altera proceeds within the quarter, while another $500 million remained payable by the end of 2027. The filing also described conditional government disbursements and $1.0 billion accrued for VLSI litigation."},{"period_end":"2025-12-27","narrative":"Intel reported $12.8 billion of capital-expenditure commitments, with a majority due within the following 12 months, and a $5.2 billion remaining Arizona SCIP contribution. The quarter also included $6.7 billion of other purchase obligations and a $900 million Mentee Robotics acquisition commitment subject to closing conditions."},{"period_end":"2026-03-28","narrative":"The $468 million Altera deferred-consideration receivable was not subject to contingencies, while $500 million remained payable by the end of 2027. Intel also disclosed $532 million of Apollo-related liquidated-damage provisions and a subsequent $14.2 billion acquisition of Apollo's Ireland SCIP interest."},{"period_end":"2026-06-27","narrative":"The $473 million Altera deferred-consideration receivable was not subject to contingencies, and $500 million remained payable by the end of 2027. The quarter also included $14.2 billion paid to reacquire Apollo's Ireland SCIP interest, $755 million of delay-related derivative liability, and $2.2 billion of expected and cumulative 2025 restructuring costs."}],"prose":{"overview":"Revenue fell 5% per year while expenses fell 1% per year, leaving less room between the two. The scale is notable against $50.5 billion of reported debt and $57.0 billion of trailing-year revenue.","debt":"Committed money matches reported debt at 1.0x. The filing identifies the full $50.5 billion of committed money as debt, with no additional lease or purchase commitments in this comparison.","wall":"The next five years bring $20.2 billion of debt maturities against just $429 million of future revenue promised for that period. That mismatch is 47.2x, while another $31.8 billion is due after year five.","flags_note":"The largest disclosed off-balance-sheet item is Intel's unrecognized $29.0 billion commitment for its share of Arizona SCIP construction costs. The filing also reports $1.7 billion of customer deposits supporting future supply and $934 million prepaid to suppliers in the same period, plus $1.5 billion of receivables sold through non-recourse factoring in the first six months of 2023."}}